    <bpmn:process id="W_W4474" name="W4474. Return-to-Duty, Return-to-Work Agreement &amp; Follow-Up Testing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Completion of rehabilitation (W4473)
Frequency: Per returning employee
Volume: Return-to-duty cases (subset of rehab cases)
Owner: Occupational Health (VS-83) / HR (VS-103) / Labor Relations (VS-84)
Participants: Occupational Health (VS-83), HR (VS-103), Labor Relations (VS-84), EAP (VS-83.3), HSE (VS-24), Legal (VS-100), Vendor (W4460)
Source: workflow W4474 — Return-to-Duty, Return-to-Work Agreement &amp; Follow-Up Testing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4474_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4474_Lane1" name="Occupational Health">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4474_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4474_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4474_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4474_Lane2" name="Labor Relations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4474_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4474_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4474_Start4" name="Completion of rehabilitation (W4473)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4474_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4474_Task5" name="return-to-duty test">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Occupational Health/HR execute a negative return-to-duty test before the employee resumes any safety-sensitive duty, and confirm fitness/clearance
Responsible (R): Occupational Health / Vendor / HR
Accountable (A): Occupational Health Lead / CHRO
Duration: Per return</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4474_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4474_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4474_Task6" name="return-to-work agreement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Labor Relations/HR/EAP put a return-to-work agreement in place — conditions, follow-up testing schedule (unannounced, per DOT-equivalent/DOLE guidance), EAP continuation, and consequences of relapse
Responsible (R): Labor Relations / HR / EAP / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO / VP Legal
Duration: Per return</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4474_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4474_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4474_Task7" name="follow-up testing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Occupational Health/HR administer the follow-up testing schedule over the defined period, monitor performance/behavior, and manage any relapse (W4471); document confidentially
Responsible (R): Occupational Health / HR / Vendor
Accountable (A): Occupational Health Lead / CHRO
Duration: Per schedule</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4474_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4474_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4474_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4474_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-682 (ensure controlled execution — Rehabilitation, Return-to-Duty, Privacy &amp; Program Analytics (PA-150.3).) | - CTL-682: negative return-to-duty test before resuming safety-sensitive duty; return-to-work agreement; scheduled unannounced follow-up testing; relapse managed (W4471)
Owner: Occupational Health (VS-83) / HR (VS-103) / Labor Relations (VS-84)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4474_Assoc10" sourceRef="W4474_Annotation9" targetRef="W4474_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
